  "notes": "West leads the ♣6 against 3♠. West's lead is won by East. East cashes a second top club and returns a third round, West ruffing. West returns a heart, won by South.\n\nThe ♠A still must be lost (the bidding marks East with that card). South must be careful not to lose a second trump trick.\n\nIf South leads a low spade to dummy's ♠K, he will immediately fail if East has a singleton ♠A as West's remaining trumps will be a certain trick.\n\nDucking the first round of trump in dummy is not a solution as East may have a doubleton ♠A. Playing the ♠K from dummy will also fail in this case as East will win the ♠A and promote another trump trick with a club return.\n\nThe solution is to cross in diamonds and lead the first round of trump from dummy. As long as East has no more than 2 spades he will be powerless to defeat the contract.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♣6 against 3♠. West's lead is won by East. East cashes a second top club and returns a third round, West ruffing. West returns a heart, won by South.",
    "The ♠A still must be lost (the bidding marks East with that card). South must be careful not to lose a second trump trick.",
    "If South leads a low spade to dummy's ♠K, he will immediately fail if East has a singleton ♠A as West's remaining trumps will be a certain trick.",
    "Ducking the first round of trump in dummy is not a solution as East may have a doubleton ♠A. Playing the ♠K from dummy will also fail in this case as East will win the ♠A and promote another trump trick with a club return.",
    "The solution is to cross in diamonds and lead the first round of trump from dummy. As long as East has no more than 2 spades he will be powerless to defeat the contract."
